    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10381" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-quā^dro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a. and n. (very
		rare). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act., to make square</i>: aurum, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 131, 14</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perticas (just before: dolare in quadrum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 3, 7</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr., to be proportioned to, to agree with, to
				square to</i> (late Lat.), <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 2,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 7 al.</span></i></div>
